From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bsp2020 <bsp2020@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:28:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/36] moe cache: a device-remap call does not re-batch a
 sibling already taken over in this round (GGML_MOE_DEVREMAP_REBATCH)

A layer whose down (or up) table was not served by the first remap call of
the layer makes its own call, and that call re-added the gate/up tables the
first call had already published.  Any decline of that launch -- a sibling
prep that declines, or a failed batched fill flush -- reset remap_n_used on
every job, so the already-published tables lost their take-over after the
scheduler had skipped their input_cpy copy: their ops read an input_cpy that
was never filled (one decode step computed with stale weights).

Skip a sibling already published in the current round.  With
GGML_MOE_FILL_BATCH_FAULT at 45/47/50/51 (and 50 + VERIFY_EVERY) the logits
are now bit-identical to the fault-free run; fault-free output unchanged.
GGML_MOE_DEVREMAP_REBATCH=1 restores the old re-batch.

(cherry picked from commit 387e8239c57389b5c85d19990aee9c5255879ce5)
(cherry picked from commit 72b8f5f4765245c6a2bbfe49609616c46fe456cd)
(cherry picked from commit 7702c3ae405a90da572bf3b9ce321c6425e996dc)
(cherry picked from commit 48a96da19bd41180c23725602736b0e77fc8208a)
(cherry picked from commit 5a8fb304c5b2dde5e0ecb5290e255676e4991d85)
(cherry picked from commit 0993a86cff52c493ca7faa00b18afdd99801aab7)
(cherry picked from commit 8b580d144493539d40c35419ea45f2afb1f1c918)
(cherry picked from commit f7645e065268c3c6f80b261981aed0a3ceac1df1)
(cherry picked from commit 0a7010341c3da7932ba933a249f26ab64c523e09)
(cherry picked from commit aeb654a75573fb8c3e1171489f6060be716900d1)
(cherry picked from commit 8d8b84dab55806c7f5027d910e53007f7db69f9d)
